# Stack docs

These npm packages do **not** ship TanStack Intent skills (except transitive `get-tsconfig`).

## Before adding dependencies or new modules

**Mandatory:** check [Astro Integrations](https://astro.build/integrations/) first.

1. Search the catalog for an official / maintained Astro integration that covers the need.
2. Prefer Official integrations and ones already in this repo (`@astrojs/react`, `@astrojs/sitemap`, `@astrojs/vercel`, `@astrojs/check`) over random npm packages.
3. If a catalog option exists, use it (or explain why the existing custom solution is better — e.g. `SeoHead` vs `astro-seo`, self-hosted fonts vs `unplugin-fonts`).
4. Only then add a non-catalog dependency — with a short justification.
5. Confirm API/version via **Astro Docs MCP** (or Context7 for non-Astro stack).

Do not propose or install Astro-related packages without this check.

## Astro (priority)

Use **Astro Docs MCP** (`Astro docs` → `https://mcp.docs.astro.build/mcp`) for routing, i18n, components, `astro check`, integrations.

Fallback: Context7 `/withastro/docs` only if Astro Docs MCP is unavailable.

## Rest of stack → Context7

| Package | Focus |
|---|---|
| `@tailwindcss/vite` / `tailwindcss` | Tailwind v4 Vite plugin, `@import "tailwindcss"` |
| `gsap` | ScrollTrigger, ticker, scrub |
| `lenis` | `autoRaf: false`, sync with GSAP |
| `typescript` | TS 6.x / `tsc` |
| `eslint` / `eslint-plugin-astro` / `typescript-eslint` | flat config |
| `@astrojs/check` | `astro check` CLI |
| `lefthook` | git hooks YAML |

`tsconfig`: `npx @tanstack/intent@latest load get-tsconfig#get-tsconfig`.

Prefer `.cursor/rules/astro.mdc` + `.cursor/skills/*` over inventing structure. No invented church copy.
